t of green elements exceeds the capacity of a column (8), only 8 elements are cleared, and the remainder persists. Initiating with the first column and transferring elements to columns 3 and 6, followed by merging the remaining elements, results in a full clearing. This pattern indicates a fundamental rule about how green elements combine and clear within the grid. This suggests a merging behavior where columns act like \"buckets\" with a fixed capacity.\n\n\n"}
